-- title:
--   Adic Galois representation at q ‖ N with U_q a unit
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N\ge 1$, and let $S_0$ be a finite set of naturals. Let $\mathcal O'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring which is a domain, adically complete for its maximal ideal and has finite residue field, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, and let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathcal O'$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}\bigl(S_2(\Gamma_0(N))\bigr)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S_0$ together with the operators $U_r$ for primes $r\mid N$ with $r\notin S_0$. Let $q$ be a prime with $q\mid N$, $q^2\nmid N$ and $q\notin S_0$ (no relation between $q$ and $p$ is assumed), and suppose $\chi(U_q)$ is a unit of $\mathcal O'$. Then there is a ring $\mathcal O''$ with the same properties (domain, discrete valuation ring, adically complete, finite residue field, characteristic zero) which is an $\mathcal O'$-algebra, module-finite over $\mathcal O'$, with $\mathcal O'\to\mathcal O''$ local and injective, and a [`GaloisRepAdic 𝒪''`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), that is a finite free $\mathcal O''$-module $V$ with $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal O''}V=2$ and a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)=(\overline{\mathbb Q}\simeq_{\mathbb Q}\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal O''}(V)$ which is adically continuous (for each $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\rho(\sigma)v-v\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O''}^n V$ for all $v$ and all $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise), such that: (i) for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$, $\ell\neq p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\chi(T_\ell)X+\ell$ (coefficients taken in $\mathcal O''$); and (ii) for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $P$ there is an $\mathcal O''$-submodule $L\subseteq V$ which is the span of $b\,0$ for some $\mathcal O''$-basis $b$ of $V$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$, such that $L$ is stable under $\rho(\sigma)$ for all $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$, $\rho(\tau)v-v\in L$ for all $v\in V$ and all $\tau$ in the image in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$, and $\rho(\sigma)v-\chi(U_q)\,v\in L$ for all $v\in V$ whenever $\sigma$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and acts on the residue field of $P$ by $x\mapsto x^{q}$.
--
--   This is the construction of the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a weight-two Hecke eigensystem, together with its local description at a prime $q$ dividing the level exactly once for which $U_q$ acts invertibly: up to a stable line, inertia at $q$ acts trivially and Frobenius at $q$ acts by $\chi(U_q)$, the shape recorded in Theorem 3.1(e),(f) of Darmon–Diamond–Taylor. The clause asserting that $\rho$ is unramified away from $Np$ is not part of the conclusion here. It is used in the comparison of the residual trace on coinvariants at $q$ with the residue of $U_q$, and in the verification of strict ordinarity at a prime of the level.
